  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What keeps pages out",
      "items": [
        "Browser tabs are sandboxed, get only the extension-API and ad-block preloads and are denied every permission but fullscreen, pointer lock and clipboard writes",
        "Every IPC channel refuses any sender but the shell view's main frame on acc://shell",
        "acc:// pages (documents, Cronsole runs, Git diffs, dev server logs, terminal_run run logs, agent session transcripts, Settings, Health, the Identity Center) run no scripts; only documents may link to documents, the rest open from the app only",
        "A file: request that names a host is refused, so no page can make Windows send an SMB sign-in"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "What an MCP client can do",
      "items": [
        "Look with no click: list_tabs, read_tab, sidebar_search, recent, list_terminals, terminal_read, run_status, cron_tasks, and tab_elements, tab_screenshot on the tab the user attached",
        "Navigate: open_tab, and open_file by Hub node id (VS Code or Explorer, never the default app)",
        "Act only after Run: terminal_run starts a managed run in its own PowerShell, whose exit code is the result; cron_run asks Cronsole's run_task; tab_click and tab_fill click or type on the attached tab"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who reaches the MCP server",
      "items": [
        "Claude Code in an app terminal: ACC_MCP_URL and ACC_MCP_TOKEN are in every terminal's environment",
        "The chat panel, through the same server and token, so its calls are logged and confirmed like any client's",
        "Every call, refused ones too, goes to the sidebar's MCP tab and logs/mcp.log, with the connecting client named; terminal_run's last 50 runs are searchable there too",
        "Contained agent sessions, through the Core's gateway, once the operator installs and pins the houston server it is registered as"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What contains an agent",
      "items": [
        "The Core starts each Claude Code or Codex session as a named identity in a Windows process container of its own (@microsoft/mxc-sdk), with its own CLI home",
        "Inside it: the workspace and what its grants open; the users folder and the Core's data folder denied; Windows' own variables only, never the user's environment",
        "No network but one host port, the session's egress proxy: tunnels only to hosts its grants allow, and only at public addresses. The same port serves its MCP gateway, with a token that dies with the session",
        "Policy is default deny: a global deny, then an explicit deny, then the narrowest allow or ask. An ask waits in the approval inbox; an unattended run treats it as deny",
        "MCP servers run as identities of their own, in containers of their own (a host or http one is marked unconfined), only once pinned. A secret reaches a server's environment only with a use grant, and results come back redacted, marked untrusted and capped",
        "An identity the operator marks broad access runs unconfined on the host, and is marked so wherever it appears"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "The window only asks",
      "items": [
        "Houston calls the Control API on a named pipe whose name and token change at every Core start; both sit in control.json in the Core's data folder, which sessions are denied. A bad token is audited and the connection closed",
